# OmniFlow — things that live in a local install but are NOT repo content.
#
# `tools/audit-push.py` publishes the repository by diffing a checkout against
# GitHub. It has its own skip list and a guard that refuses to run outside a real
# checkout (running it from ~/.omni-flow once published this exact working data —
# see CHANGELOG 0.2.2). This file is the second line of defence, for anyone using
# plain git instead.

# —— Local working data: your maps and the vault state ——
graphs/
templates/
tree.json
crosslinks.json
live-conversation.json
WORKLOG.txt
trash/
.bak/

# —— OS / editor noise ——
.DS_Store
*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
